  "knowledgePattern": "Reflect one endpoint to turn a broken route into a straight one",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Reflect one endpoint",
      "body": "<p>Draw the perpendicular from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> and find where they meet. Place the reflected point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></math> the same distance beyond that meeting point.</p>",
      "recap": "Reflection preserves distances to points on the mirror line.",
      "pitfall": "Reflect the point across the sloping line, not across an axis.",
      "pause": "Find the coordinates of the reflected point.",
      "recall": []
    },
    {
      "title": "Straighten the path",
      "body": "<p>For a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math> on the mirror line, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></math>. Replace the broken path by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math> and compare it with the straight segment from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "A shortest-length answer needs both a lower bound and a route attaining it.",
      "pitfall": "Check that the straight segment actually crosses the allowed line.",
      "pause": "Calculate the distance and check the crossing.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b3-l06",
          "reminder": "A shortest-length answer needs both a lower bound and a route attaining it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> Reflect A in the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. The perpendicular through A is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, which meets the line at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. This is the midpoint of A and its reflection <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> For any P on the mirror line, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>: the perpendicular midpoint construction gives congruent right triangles. Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> The straight segment from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> crosses the mirror line at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, so the lower bound is attained by an allowed P.</p><p><strong>4.</strong> The minimum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>&#x02032;</mi></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>, answer E. The crossing lies between the segment endpoints, so no extra backtracking length is needed.</p>"
}
